# ============================================================================
# ADEENA TRADERS - Frontend production build
# ============================================================================
# Vite reads this file during `npm run build`, so the deployed app knows where
# the API lives without anything being configured in the hosting dashboard.
#
# This is committed on purpose. Every VITE_* value is compiled into the
# JavaScript bundle and is therefore public to anyone who opens the site - so
# an API URL belongs here, and a secret never does.
#
# A real environment variable set in the host's dashboard overrides this file,
# which is how you point a fork or a staging build somewhere else without
# editing the repository.
#
# Because the value is baked in at build time, changing it requires a REDEPLOY,
# not just a restart.

# The API is reached through THIS site's own domain: vercel.json rewrites
# /api/* and /uploads/* to https://adeena-trader-backend.vercel.app. Going
# through the same domain makes the sign-in cookie first-party. Called directly
# across two vercel.app sites it is a third-party cookie, which Safari (every
# iPhone) blocks by default - staff were signed out on every reload.
#
# To call a backend directly instead, set a full URL here, e.g.
#   VITE_API_URL=https://adeena-trader-backend.vercel.app/api
VITE_API_URL=/api

# Only needed when uploaded files are served from somewhere other than the API
# host (a CDN, an object-storage bucket). Left unset, uploads resolve against
# the same domain, which the rewrite above forwards to the backend.
# VITE_FILE_URL=
